.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt WDPMCD.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm wdpmcd.conf
.Nd configuration file for wdpmcd
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Xr wdpmcd 8
configuration file contains one
.Ar key No = Ar value
setting per line.
Blank lines are ignored, and everything from a
.Ql #
to the end of the line is a comment.
Unknown keys, malformed values and values outside the stated range make the
whole file invalid.
.Pp
Times are in seconds and may have a fractional part.
Temperatures are in degrees Celsius.
.Sh SETTINGS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm device
Serial device of the PMC.
By default it is found by its PCI identity, 8086:228c.
.It Cm pidfile
Pidfile; the
.Fl p
option overrides it.
.It Cm interval
Time between sensor reads and fan updates, 0.1 to 3600.
The default is 10.
.It Cm watchdog
Seconds the loop may go without finishing an iteration before the kernel ends
the process, 15 to 600.
It must be at least twice
.Cm interval
plus
.Cm pmc_timeout ,
so a slow but healthy cycle is not mistaken for a hang.
The supervisor starts
.Xr wdpmcd 8
again, and start-up sets the safe maximum.
The default is 60.
.It Cm disk_interval
Time between disk temperature reads, 0.1 to 86400.
It is never shorter than
.Cm interval .
The default is 30.
.It Cm safe_max
Duty cycle in percent used after any fault and at exit, 30 to 99.
It must not be below
.Cm min_duty .
The default is 99.
.It Cm min_duty
Lowest duty cycle the curve may produce, 30 to 99.
The default is 30, which is also the absolute limit.
.It Cm status_interval
Time between reads of the PMC power supply and drive presence registers, 0.5 to 86400.
Changes are logged to syslog.
0 turns status monitoring off.
The default is 10.
.It Cm drive_bays
Number of drive bays reported, 1 to 4.
The default is 2.
.It Cm metrics_dir
Directory in which a node_exporter textfile collector file is written atomically
after every status read.
By default no file is written.
.It Cm metrics_file
Name of that file, a plain name ending in
.Ql .prom .
The default is
.Pa wdpmcd.prom .
.It Cm min_rpm
A fan slower than this is treated as a fault.
The default is 400.
.It Cm led
Control the front-panel power LED, yes or no.
The default is yes.
.It Cm led_starting , led_up , led_fault , led_pool , led_shutdown
How the LED looks while starting (blinking blue), when up (steady blue), on
a fan fail-safe (blinking red), on a degraded pool (steady red) and after a
clean stop (blinking blue).
A value is a colour, one of off, blue, red, green or yellow, optionally
followed by steady, blink or pulse.
Every colour works steadily or blinking.
The pulse register carries one bit, so pulse belongs to blue and any other
colour with pulse is an error.
.It Cm pool_cmd
Program run as
.Ql pool_cmd list -H -o health
to find out whether a pool is not ONLINE.
The value none disables the check.
The default is /sbin/zpool on FreeBSD and /usr/sbin/zpool elsewhere.
.It Cm pool_interval
Time between pool checks (health and capacity), 0.1 to 86400.
The default is 60.
.It Cm capacity_cmd
Program run as
.Ql capacity_cmd list -H -o capacity .
While any pool is fuller than
.Cm capacity_limit
the LED shows
.Cm led_capacity
(steady red, as the stock firmware does).
On by default; the value none disables it.
A query that fails never counts as a fault.
.It Cm capacity_limit
Percent, 1 to 100.
The default is 95.
.It Cm led_capacity , led_ups
Looks for a nearly full pool and for a UPS on battery.
The default for both is steady red.
.It Cm ups_cmd
A program and arguments, run without a shell, that prints the UPS status.
The word OB (NUT) or ONBATT (apcupsd) means on battery and shows
.Cm led_ups .
There is no default; without it the UPS state is inert.
.It Cm ups_interval
Time between UPS checks, 0.1 to 86400.
The default is 15.
.It Cm disk
A disk to monitor with
.Xr smartctl 8 .
May be repeated.
The hottest disk is used.
.Ql none
turns disk monitoring off.
The default is
.Pa /dev/ada0
and
.Pa /dev/ada1
on
.Fx ,
.Pa /dev/sda
and
.Pa /dev/sdb
on Linux.
Disks in standby are not woken; they are assumed to be at least 35 degrees.
.It Cm smartctl
Path of
.Xr smartctl 8 .
.It Cm smartctl_timeout
Time allowed for one
.Xr smartctl 8
run, 0.1 to 60.
The default is 5.
.It Cm cpu_temp_file
Read the CPU temperature, in millidegrees, from this file instead of
.Va dev.cpu.N.temperature
.Pq Fx
or the hwmon
.Ql coretemp
driver
.Pq Linux .
.It Cm sysctl_cmd
Program run as
.Ql sysctl_cmd -n hw.ncpu
once, and then as
.Ql sysctl_cmd -n dev.cpu.0.temperature dev.cpu.1.temperature ...
to read the CPU temperature of every core on
.Fx ,
because the daemon itself makes no
.Xr sysctl 3
calls.
The hottest core counts.
A missing or unparsable value, or a helper that does not answer in time,
counts as a failed CPU reading.
The default is /sbin/sysctl.
.It Cm syslog_socket
Path of the
.Xr syslogd 8
datagram socket.
The default is
.Pa /var/run/log
on
.Fx
and
.Pa /dev/log
elsewhere.
.It Cm link_if
Interface whose carrier is watched, for example
.Ql re0 .
When it goes down the LED shows
.Cm led_link .
The default is
.Ql re0
on
.Fx ;
it is off elsewhere until set.
.It Cm led_link
Look for a network link that has no carrier.
The default is steady red.
.It Cm ifconfig_cmd
Program run as
.Ql ifconfig_cmd link_if
to read the carrier state on
.Fx .
Output that says neither
.Ql status: active
nor
.Ql status: no carrier
is ignored and keeps the previous verdict.
The default is /sbin/ifconfig.
.It Cm curve
One step of the fan curve:
.Ar duty cpu disk pmc .
The step applies when any of the CPU, disk or PMC temperatures reaches its
limit; the highest applicable step wins.
May be repeated.
Duties must be between 30 and 99 and rise strictly from line to line.
Below the first step the fan runs at
.Cm min_duty .
The default is
.Bd -literal -offset indent
curve = 45 50 40 45
curve = 60 60 44 50
curve = 80 70 48 55
curve = 99 80 52 60
.Ed
.It Cm hysteresis
Degrees below a step's limits that every sensor must be before the fan may
slow down from that step, 0 to 20.
The default is 3.
.It Cm drop_step
Largest decrease of the duty cycle at one time, in percentage points.
The default is 15.
.It Cm drop_interval
Least time between decreases, 0 to 3600.
The default is 30.
.It Cm pmc_timeout
Time allowed for one exchange with the PMC, 0.1 to 30.
The default is 5.
.It Cm rpm_delay
Time between setting the fan and checking its speed, 0 to 60.
The default is 2.
.It Cm startup_settle
Time at the safe maximum after start, 0 to 120.
The default is 6.
.It Cm discover_timeout
Time to wait for the PMC UART to appear at boot, 0 to 600.
The default is 20.
.It Cm max_failures
The daemon exits, for its supervisor to restart, after this many
consecutive cycles in which the PMC did not accept a fan setting.
The default is 30.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa /usr/local/etc/wdpmcd.conf.sample" -compact
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/wdpmcd.conf
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/wdpmcd.conf.sample
.It Pa /etc/wdpmcd.conf
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr wdpmcd 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Rei Walker
